{
  "Same species. Different bodies.": "<div class=\"split\"><div><h2>Same species.<br>Different bodies.</h2><p class=\"lead\">Notice the head<br>relative to the body.</p></div><figure class=\"worker-plate\"><div class=\"plate-window\"><img src=\"site/ants/public-worker-sizes.jpg\" alt=\"Side-by-side photographs of a major and a minor Camponotus boghossiani worker, showing different head proportions\"></div><div class=\"pair-labels\"><span>Larger worker \u00b7 major</span><span>Smaller worker \u00b7 minor</span></div><figcaption><i>Camponotus boghossiani</i> \u00b7 preserved specimens \u00b7 top row of source plate<br><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.899.46933\">Salata et al. 2019</a> \u00b7 CC BY 4.0 \u00b7 displayed crop<br>Separate scale bars: compare body shape, not a measured size ratio.</figcaption></figure></div>",
  "Which head fits the job?": "<style>.public-head-game .card-photo img{object-fit:contain}.public-head-game [data-answer=army] .front img{transform:scale(1.7);transform-origin:28% 30%}.public-head-game [data-answer=door] .front img{transform:scale(2.1);transform-origin:35% 57%}.public-head-game .photo-credit{font-size:13px}.public-head-game .back>img{object-fit:contain}</style><div class=\"head-game public-head-game\"><h2 id=\"title-13\">Which head fits the job?</h2><p class=\"game-instruction\">Choose a job, then a head. Or flip a card to explore.</p><div class=\"job-choices\" aria-label=\"Choose a purpose\"><button data-job=\"door\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Plug the entrance</button><button data-job=\"trap\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Snap up prey</button><button data-job=\"army\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Guard the colony</button></div><div class=\"head-cards\"><article class=\"head-card\" data-answer=\"army\"><button class=\"card-flip\" aria-label=\"Flip head A\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><span class=\"card-face front\"><span class=\"card-photo live-head\"><img src=\"site/ants/public-army-soldier.jpg\" alt=\"Preserved Eciton hamatum soldier: profile detail showing long hooked jaws\"></span><span class=\"card-letter\">Head A <small>Flip to meet the ant \u2197</small></span></span><span class=\"card-face back\" hidden><img src=\"site/ants/public-army-soldier.jpg\" alt=\"Preserved Eciton hamatum soldier, whole body\"><span class=\"card-answer\">Guard the colony</span><i>Eciton hamatum</i><span class=\"card-detail\">Hooked jaws on an army-ant soldier.</span></span></button></article><article class=\"head-card\" data-answer=\"door\"><button class=\"card-flip\" aria-label=\"Flip head B\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><span class=\"card-face front\"><span class=\"card-photo live-head\"><img src=\"site/ants/public-door-worker.jpg\" alt=\"Living Colobopsis truncata worker: profile detail showing the blunt head\"></span><span class=\"card-letter\">Head B <small>Flip to meet the ant \u2197</small></span></span><span class=\"card-face back\" hidden><img src=\"site/ants/public-door-worker.jpg\" alt=\"Living Colobopsis truncata ant, whole body\"><span class=\"card-answer\">Plug the entrance</span><i>Colobopsis truncata</i><span class=\"card-detail\">A blunt head closes the twig-nest entrance.</span></span></button></article><article class=\"head-card\" data-answer=\"trap\"><button class=\"card-flip\" aria-label=\"Flip head C\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><span class=\"card-face front\"><span class=\"card-photo live-head\"><img src=\"site/ants/public-trap-head.jpg\" alt=\"Preserved Odontomachus bauri worker head with long jaws\"></span><span class=\"card-letter\">Head C <small>Flip to meet the ant \u2197</small></span></span><span class=\"card-face back\" hidden><img src=\"site/ants/public-trap-whole.jpg\" alt=\"Preserved Odontomachus bauri worker, whole body\"><span class=\"card-answer\">Snap up prey</span><i>Odontomachus bauri</i><span class=\"card-detail\">Spring-loaded jaws; also used in escape jumps.</span></span></button></article></div><div class=\"game-bottom\"><p id=\"matchStatus\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">0 of 3 matched \u00b7 No job selected.</p><div><button id=\"revealHeads\">Reveal all</button><button id=\"resetHeads\">Start again</button></div></div><p class=\"photo-credit\">Head details on fronts, whole ants on reverse \u00b7 Door ant: live photograph, Volker Borovsky \u00b7 Army ant: Will Ericson / AntWeb \u00b7 Trap-jaw: April Nobile / AntWeb \u00b7 Army and trap-jaw images are preserved specimens. Full licenses in credits.</p></div>",
  "How many neighbors make a decision?": "<style>@media(min-width:801px) and (max-height:780px){.public-quorum .sim canvas{height:28vh;min-height:200px}.public-quorum>.footnote{font-size:15px;margin-top:12px}}</style><div class=\"public-quorum\"><div class=\"sim-heading\"><h2>How many neighbors<br>make a decision?</h2><p class=\"lead\">A colony needs a new home.</p></div><div class=\"sim\"><canvas id=\"quorumCanvas\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scouts inspect two candidate nests. Reaching a local threshold starts transport.\">Scouts compare two nests. Read their numbers and the decision below.</canvas><div class=\"controls\"><button id=\"quorumPlay\">Start scouts</button><button id=\"quorumStep\">One assessment</button><button id=\"quorumReset\">New search</button><label for=\"threshold\">Threshold <output id=\"thresholdValue\">8</output><input id=\"threshold\" type=\"range\" min=\"3\" max=\"12\" value=\"8\"></label></div><p class=\"sim-status\" id=\"quorumStatus\">Near / exposed: 0 \u00b7 Far / sheltered: 0 \u00b7 Searching</p></div><p class=\"footnote\">Toy model inspired by <i>Temnothorax</i> nest choice. Counts and thresholds are invented for teaching; not a local-species claim.</p><p class=\"footnote\"><a href=\"https://pratt.lab.asu.edu/videos\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Watch actual nest-search recruitment &amp; nestmate transport \u2197</a> \u00b7 Stephen Pratt / Arizona State University \u00b7 internet needed</p></div>",
  "Living ladders": "<div class=\"film-layout\"><div><h2 id=\"title-10\">Living ladders</h2><p class=\"lead\">Some ants become<br>the structure.</p><p class=\"watch-cue\">Watch the lower panel.<br>Which ants stop moving?</p></div><figure><video id=\"scaffoldVideo\" controls muted playsinline preload=\"none\" aria-label=\"Research timelapse of Eciton burchellii ants assembling scaffolds at 50 and 90 degree slopes\"><source src=\"https://www.uni-konstanz.de/fileadmin/pi/fileserver/2021_EXTRA/learning_about_system_stability_from_ants_image_matthew_lutz_video_matthew_lutz_chris_reid_simon_garnier_and_iain_couzin.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"><track kind=\"captions\" src=\"site/ants/scaffolds.vtt\" srclang=\"en\" label=\"English description\" default></video><figcaption>Internet needed \u00b7 university-hosted film<br>15-second research timelapse \u00b7 40\u00d7 speed \u00b7 <i>Eciton burchellii</i><br><a href=\"https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/722631\">Lutz, Reid, Garnier & Couzin / University of Konstanz</a></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"footnote\">Researchers call these \u201cscaffolds.\u201d Stationary ants provide footholds on a slope. A wider-world example.</p>",
  "Image &amp; film credits 1": "<h2>Image &amp; film credits <span class=\"credit-page\">1</span></h2><div class=\"source-columns media-columns\"><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Formica_integroides_worker_ant.jpg\">Formica integroides worker ant.jpg</a><br>Alex Wild<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Formica_integroides_worker_ant.jpg\">CC0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Closeup_on_honeypot_ants_(Myrmecocystus_mimicus)_at_Oakland_Zoo.jpg\">Closeup on honeypot ants (Myrmecocystus mimicus) at Oakland Zoo.jpg</a><br>Derrick Coetzee (User:Dcoetzee)<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Closeup_on_honeypot_ants_(Myrmecocystus_mimicus)_at_Oakland_Zoo.jpg\">CC0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Shasta,_Lake_Siskiyou,_SW_view.jpg\">Mount Shasta, Lake Siskiyou, SW view.jpg</a><br>Radomianin<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Shasta,_Lake_Siskiyou,_SW_view.jpg\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p></div><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Flicker_(red-shafted).jpg\">Northern Flicker (red-shafted).jpg</a><br>Wildreturn<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Flicker_(red-shafted).jpg\">CC BY 2.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trillium_ovatum_1290.JPG\">Trillium ovatum 1290.JPG</a><br>Walter Siegmund (talk)<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trillium_ovatum_1290.JPG\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ants_collecting_honeydew_drops_01.jpg\">Ants collecting honeydew drops 01.jpg</a><br>Hexafluoride<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ants_collecting_honeydew_drops_01.jpg\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p></div></div>",
  "Image &amp; film credits 2": "<h2>Image &amp; film credits <span class=\"credit-page\">2</span></h2><div class=\"source-columns media-columns\"><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leafcutter_ants.webm\">Leafcutter ants.webm</a><br>Filo g\u00e8n&#x27;<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leafcutter_ants.webm\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modoc.jpg\">Modoc.jpg</a><br>Alex Wild<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modoc.jpg\">CC0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scheme_ant_worker_anatomy-en.svg\">Scheme ant worker anatomy-en.svg</a><br>Mariana Ruiz (LadyofHats)<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scheme_ant_worker_anatomy-en.svg\">Public domain</a></p></div><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camponotus_mutilarius_(xiangban).jpg\">Camponotus mutilarius (xiangban).jpg</a><br>Photographer uncredited<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camponotus_mutilarius_(xiangban).jpg\">Public domain</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ant,_St_michaels,_jan_reese,_talbot,_waxwing,_side_2016-07-19-13.44_(28723205391).jpg\">Ant, St michaels, jan reese, talbot, waxwing, side 2016-07-19-13.44 (28723205391).jpg</a><br>USGS Bee Inventory &amp; Monitoring Lab<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ant,_St_michaels,_jan_reese,_talbot,_waxwing,_side_2016-07-19-13.44_(28723205391).jpg\">Public domain</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ant_life_cycle.jpg\">Ant life cycle.jpg</a><br>ASU Ask A Biologist, http://askabiologist.asu.edu<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a></p></div></div>",
  "Image &amp; film credits 3": "<h2>Image &amp; film credits <span class=\"credit-page\">3</span></h2><div class=\"source-columns media-columns\"><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atta_laevigata_fungus_garden.jpg\">Atta laevigata fungus garden.jpg</a><br>Alex Wild<br><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\">CC0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Formica_sibylla_casent0005374_profile_1.jpg\">Formica sibylla casent0005374 profile 1.jpg</a><br>AntWeb / California Academy of Sciences<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\">CC BY 4.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pavement_ants_battling_on_sidewalk_-_medium_closeup.jpg\">Pavement ants battling on sidewalk - medium closeup.jpg</a><br>Chetvorno<br><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\">CC0</a></p></div><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/722631\">Army-ant scaffolds: timelapse at 50 and 90 degrees</a><br>Matthew Lutz, Chris Reid, Simon Garnier and Iain Couzin / University of Konstanz<br><a href=\"https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/722631\">Official university-hosted stream \u00b7 rights retained by creators</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scheme_ant_worker_anatomy-clean.svg\">Scheme ant worker anatomy-clean.svg</a><br>LadyofHats (original version); Sophivorus (clean version)<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scheme_ant_worker_anatomy-clean.svg\">Public domain</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Two_ants_fighting_at_Coalseam_Conservation_Park,_August_2022_04.jpg\">Two ants fighting at Coalseam Conservation Park, August 2022 04.jpg</a><br>Calistemon<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p></div></div>",
  "Image &amp; film credits 4": "<h2>Image &amp; film credits <span class=\"credit-page\">4</span></h2><div class=\"source-columns media-columns\"><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.20185.006\">A recruiter lays three scent marks \u00b7 research film</a><br>Ehud Fonio, Yael Heyman, Lucas Boczkowski, Aviram Gelblum, Ayal Ayali, Amos Korman &amp; Ofer Feinerman<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">CC BY 4.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://www.kyushu-u.ac.jp/en/researches/view/360\">Parasitic takeover \u00b7 Kyushu University film preview</a><br>Kyushu University; research by Taku Shimada, Yuji Tanaka &amp; Keizo Takasuka<br><a href=\"https://www.kyushu-u.ac.jp/en/researches/view/360\">Official YouTube embed \u00b7 rights retained by creators</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"http://blog.livedoor.jp/antroom/archives/51997207.html\">Chemical takeover: queen sprayed</a><br>Taku Shimada / AntRoom<br><a href=\"http://blog.livedoor.jp/antroom/archives/51997207.html\">Official YouTube embed \u00b7 rights retained by creator</a></p></div><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"http://blog.livedoor.jp/antroom/archives/51997207.html\">Chemical takeover: host workers react</a><br>Taku Shimada / AntRoom<br><a href=\"http://blog.livedoor.jp/antroom/archives/51997207.html\">Official YouTube embed \u00b7 rights retained by creator</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colobopsis_truncata_worker.jpg\">Door-head worker \u00b7 Colobopsis truncata</a><br>Volker Borovsky<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casent0612205_p_1_high.jpg\">Army-ant soldier \u00b7 Eciton hamatum</a><br>Will Ericson / AntWeb, California Academy of Sciences<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">CC BY 4.0</a></p></div></div>",
  "Image &amp; film credits 5": "<h2>Image &amp; film credits <span class=\"credit-page\">5</span></h2><div class=\"source-columns media-columns\"><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camponotus_(10.3897-zookeys.899.46933)_Figures_11%E2%80%9316.jpg\">Camponotus (10.3897-zookeys.899.46933) Figures 11\u201316.jpg</a><br>Salata S, Loss AC, Karaman C, Kiran K, Borowiec L (2019) Review of the Camponotus kiesenwetteri group (Hymenoptera, Formicidae) in the Aegean with the description of a new species. ZooKeys 899: 85-107. https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.899.46933<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\">CC BY 4.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Odontomachus_bauri_casent0172629_profile_1.jpg\">Trap-jaw worker \u00b7 Odontomachus bauri</a><br>April Nobile / AntWeb, California Academy of Sciences<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">CC BY 4.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Odontomachus_bauri_casent0172629_head_1.jpg\">Odontomachus bauri casent0172629 head 1.jpg</a><br>April Nobile / AntWeb, California Academy of Sciences<br><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\">CC BY 4.0</a></p></div><div></div></div>"
